 ["The spot USD/EUR exchange rate is 1.2000. The one-year interest rate is 4% for the US dollar and 2% for the euro. The one-year forward rate is closest to:", ["1.1769", "1.2000", "1.2235"], 2, "Forward = 1.2000 × 1.04 / 1.02 = 1.2235. The dollar interest rate goes in the numerator because the dollar is the price currency."],
 ["The spot exchange rate is 1.2000 and the three-month forward quote is +25 points. The forward exchange rate is closest to:", ["1.2003", "1.2025", "1.2250"], 1, "For a four-decimal quote, 25 points equal 0.0025, so the forward rate is 1.2025."],
 ["A currency with a higher interest rate than another currency will trade against it in the forward market at a:", ["discount.", "premium.", "rate equal to the spot rate."], 0, "The forward discount offsets the interest advantage, so that no riskless profit is available."],
 ["The spot USD/EUR exchange rate is 1.2000 and the one-year forward rate is 1.2235. The euro is trading at a forward:", ["discount of 1.92%.", "premium of 1.96%.", "premium of 2.35%."], 1, "1.2235 / 1.2000 − 1 = 1.96%. The base currency, the euro, costs more forward than spot, so it is at a premium."],
 ["The spot MXN/USD exchange rate is 20.000. Annualized 90-day interest rates are 8% for the peso and 4% for the US dollar. Using a 360-day year, the 90-day forward rate is closest to:", ["19.804", "20.198", "20.769"], 1, "20.000 × (1 + 0.08 × 90/360) / (1 + 0.04 × 90/360) = 20.000 × 1.02 / 1.01 = 20.198."],
 ["The forward exchange rate between two currencies is determined primarily by the:", ["expected future spot exchange rate.", "difference in their interest rates.", "difference in their trade balances."], 1, "The no-arbitrage forward rate depends only on the spot rate and the two interest rates for the period."],
 ["A dealer quotes a cross rate that differs from the rate implied by the two currencies' exchange rates against the US dollar. This situation most likely creates an opportunity for:", ["hedging.", "speculation.", "triangular arbitrage."], 2, "Trading round the three currency pairs locks in a riskless profit until the quotes come back into line."],
 ["The spot exchange rate is 1.5000 and the one-year forward quote is +2.0%. The forward exchange rate is closest to:", ["1.5002", "1.5020", "1.5300"], 2, "A percentage forward quote is applied to the spot rate: 1.5000 × 1.02 = 1.5300."],
